content:
PLAN:
Adjust the CSS styles related to spacing in the UI components to improve consistency and visual balance. This includes updating margins and paddings in the main UI container and key elements to fix spacing issues.

FILES TO CHANGE:
- src/styles/ui.css

FULL FILE CONTENT:
### src/styles/ui.css
```css
/* UI Spacing Fixes */

.ui-container {
  padding: 20px; /* increased padding for better spacing */
  margin: 0 auto;
  max-width: 1200px;
}

.ui-header {
  margin-bottom: 24px; /* added space below header */
}

.ui-section {
  margin-bottom: 32px; /* consistent spacing between sections */
  padding: 16px;
}

.ui-button {
  padding: 10px 20px; /* balanced button padding */
  margin-right: 12px;
}

.ui-input {
  padding: 8px 12px;
  margin-bottom: 16px;
  width: 100%;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
```

RUN COMMANDS:
- npm run build
- npm start

EXPECTED OUTPUT:
- UI elements have consistent and visually balanced spacing.
- Sections and buttons no longer appear cramped or unevenly spaced.
- Overall improved readability and user experience.

TROUBLESHOOTING:
- If spacing still appears off, inspect elements with browser dev tools to identify overridden styles.
- Check for conflicting CSS rules or inline styles that may affect spacing.
- Verify that the updated CSS file is properly loaded and not cached.
